1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,184
Hello,

2
00:00:00,184 --> 00:00:01,880
and welcome to Focus on the Arts.

3
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:06,710
I'm your host - Dave Green - and this is your very own local radio programme.

4
00:00:06,710 --> 00:00:11,755
Every Friday evening we put the spotlight on different arts and culture facilities,

5
00:00:11,755 --> 00:00:14,609
and look at the shows and events that are on offer in the coming

6
00:00:14,609 --> 00:00:14,890
week.

7
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:18,400
And today the focus is on The National Arts Centre.

8
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:22,939
Now, if you don't already know it yourself, I'm sure you've all heard of

9
00:00:22,939 --> 00:00:23,000
it.

10
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,430
It's famous throughout the world as one of the major venues for classical music.

11
00:00:27,430 --> 00:00:30,995
But did you know that it is actually much more than just a place

12
00:00:30,995 --> 00:00:31,760
to hear concerts?

13
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:36,348
The Centre itself is a huge complex that caters for a great range of

14
00:00:36,348 --> 00:00:36,630
arts.

15
00:00:36,630 --> 00:00:42,605
Under a single roof it houses concert rooms, theatres, cinemas, art galleries

16
00:00:42,605 --> 00:00:48,038
and a wonderful public library, as well as service facilities including three restaurants

17
00:00:48,038 --> 00:00:48,680
and a bookshop.

18
00:00:48,680 --> 00:00:53,480
So at any one time, the choice of entertainment there is simply enormous.

19
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:58,635
So, how did they manage to build such a big arts complex right in

20
00:00:58,635 --> 00:00:59,400
the heart of the city?

21
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:04,650
Well, the area was completely destroyed by bombs during the war in 1940.

22
00:01:04,650 --> 00:01:09,237
So the opportunity was taken to create a cultural centre that would be, what

23
00:01:09,237 --> 00:01:09,780
they called:

24
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:11,550
'the City's gift to the Nation'.

25
00:01:11,550 --> 00:01:15,362
Of course it took a while for such a big project to get started,

26
00:01:15,362 --> 00:01:18,251
but it was planned in the 60s, built in the 70s

27
00:01:18,251 --> 00:01:21,300
and eventually opened to the public in 1983.

28
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:25,100
Ever since then it has proved to be a great success.

29
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:29,162
It is not privately owned, like many arts centres,

30
00:01:29,162 --> 00:01:32,620
but is still in public hands - it's run by the City Council.

31
00:01:32,620 --> 00:01:38,157
Both our National Symphony Orchestra and National Theatre Company were involved in the planning

32
00:01:38,157 --> 00:01:38,739
of the project,

33
00:01:38,739 --> 00:01:42,290
and they are now based there - giving regular performances every week -

34
00:01:42,290 --> 00:01:47,363
and as the Centre is open 363 days of the year, there are plenty

35
00:01:47,363 --> 00:01:48,530
of performances to choose from.

36
00:01:48,530 --> 00:01:51,541
So, to give you some idea of what's on,

37
00:01:51,541 --> 00:01:55,356
and to help you choose from the many possibilities, we've made a selection of

38
00:01:55,356 --> 00:01:56,400
the star attractions.

39
00:01:56,400 --> 00:02:02,673
If you're interested in classical music, then we recommend you go along to the National on either Monday

40
00:02:02,673 --> 00:02:08,045
or Tuesday evening at 7.30 for a spectacular production of 'The Magic Flute' -

41
00:02:08,045 --> 00:02:10,430
probably the most popular of all Mozart's operas.

42
00:02:10,430 --> 00:02:15,131
It's in the Garden Hall and tickets start at only ￡8.00,

43
00:02:15,131 --> 00:02:17,040
but you'll have to be early if you want to get them that cheap!

44
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:20,400
And remember, it's only on for those two evenings.

45
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:24,520
For those more interested in the cinema, you might like to see the new

46
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:28,800
Canadian film which is showing on Wednesday evening at 8pm in Cinema 2.

47
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:34,448
And that's called 'Three Lives.' It's had fantastic reviews and tickets cost just ￡4.50

48
00:02:34,448 --> 00:02:34,498
,

49
00:02:34,498 --> 00:02:38,590
which is a reduction on the usual price of ￡5.50.

50
00:02:38,590 --> 00:02:42,400
So, it's really good value, especially for such a great movie.

51
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:46,128
But you can see the centre's main attraction at the weekend,

52
00:02:46,128 --> 00:02:50,872
because on Saturday and Sunday, 11 am to 10 pm, they're showing a wonderful

53
00:02:50,872 --> 00:02:54,600
new exhibition that hasn't been seen anywhere else in Europe yet.

54
00:02:54,600 --> 00:03:00,200
It's a collection of Chinese Art called 'Faces of China' - that's in Gallery 1 -

55
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:05,800
and it has some really fascinating paintings and sculptures by leading artists from all

56
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:06,600
over China -

57
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:09,714
and the good news is that it is completely free,

58
00:03:09,714 --> 00:03:10,960
so don't miss it!

59
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:15,419
So why not go along to the National Arts Centre next week for one -

60
00:03:15,419 --> 00:03:17,330
or all - of these great events -

61
00:03:17,330 --> 00:03:21,773
and you can always pick up a programme and check out all the other performances

62
00:03:21,773 --> 00:03:22,958
and exhibitions on offer,

63
00:03:22,958 --> 00:03:25,920
or coming soon, on almost every day of the year.

64
00:03:25,920 --> 00:03:29,800
Next week we'll be looking at the new Museum of Science...
